{"name":"Cherokee Red","hex":"#824e4a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cherokee","blocks":[{"text":"The Cherokee or Tsalagi people are one of the Indigenous peoples of the Southeastern Woodlands of the United States. Prior to the 18th century, they were concentrated in their ancestral homelands, living in towns along river valleys in what is now southwestern North Carolina, southeastern Tennessee, southwestern Virginia, parts of western South Carolina, northern Georgia, and northeastern Alabama, with hunting grounds extending into Kentucky. Together, these lands encompassed approximately 40,000 square miles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Henry_Inman_-_Sequoyah_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/330px-Henry_Inman_-_Sequoyah_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherokee"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Mound_Builder_City.jpeg/500px-Mound_Builder_City.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Mound_Builder_City.jpeg/500px-Mound_Builder_City.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMound_Builder_City.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Smoky_Mtn_View.jpg/500px-Smoky_Mtn_View.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Smoky_Mtn_View.jpg/1280px-Smoky_Mtn_View.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Smoky_Mtn_View.jpg/500px-Smoky_Mtn_View.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Great Smoky Mountains","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASmoky_Mtn_View.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Indians_NW_of_South_Carolina.jpg/500px-Indians_NW_of_South_Carolina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Indians_NW_of_South_Carolina.jpg/1280px-Indians_NW_of_South_Carolina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Indians_NW_of_South_Carolina.jpg/500px-Indians_NW_of_South_Carolina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An annotated copy of a hand-painted Catawba deerskin map of the tribes between Charleston (left) and Virginia (right) following the displacements of a century of disease and slavery among the indigenous peoples of the Americas and the 1715–7 Yamasee War. The Cherokee are labelled as \"Cherrikies\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIndians_NW_of_South_Carolina.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Three_Cherokee.jpg/500px-Three_Cherokee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Three_Cherokee.jpg/500px-Three_Cherokee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"After the Anglo-Cherokee War, bitterness remained between the two groups. In 1765, Henry Timberlake took three Cherokee chiefs to London meet the Crown and help strengthen the newly declared peace.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThree_Cherokee.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Mather_Brown_-_Portrait_of_Major_John_Norton_as_Mohawk_Chief_Teyoninhokarawen_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Mather_Brown_-_Portrait_of_Major_John_Norton_as_Mohawk_Chief_Teyoninhokarawen_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Mather_Brown_-_Portrait_of_Major_John_Norton_as_Mohawk_Chief_Teyoninhokarawen_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/1280px-Mather_Brown_-_Portrait_of_Major_John_Norton_as_Mohawk_Chief_Teyoninhokarawen_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Mather_Brown_-_Portrait_of_Major_John_Norton_as_Mohawk_Chief_Teyoninhokarawen_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Mather_Brown_-_Portrait_of_Major_John_Norton_as_Mohawk_Chief_Teyoninhokarawen_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?